> sqrtmod 0 7
x^2 = 0 mod 7: x = 0
  how: directly
  check: 0^2 = 0 (mod 7); brute force over 0..6: 1 solution
> sqrtmod 2 7
x^2 = 2 mod 7: x = 3, 4
  how: p = 3 mod 4: x = a^((p+1)/4)
  check: 3^2 = 2, 4^2 = 2 (mod 7); brute force over 0..6: 2 solutions
> sqrtmod 3 7
x^2 = 3 mod 7: no solution (3 is not a square mod 7)
  how: Euler's criterion (a square mod an odd prime p has a^((p-1)/2) = 1)
  check: Euler's criterion 3^((7-1)/2) = 6 != 1; brute force over 0..6: 0 solutions
> sqrtmod 1 8
x^2 = 1 mod 8: x = 1, 3, 5, 7
  how: 8 = 2^3: roots mod each prime (Tonelli-Shanks), lifted to the prime powers (Hensel), combined by CRT
  check: 1^2 = 1, 3^2 = 1, 5^2 = 1, 7^2 = 1 (mod 8); brute force over 0..7: 4 solutions
> sqrtmod 1 15
x^2 = 1 mod 15: x = 1, 4, 11, 14
  how: 15 = 3 * 5: roots mod each prime (Tonelli-Shanks), lifted to the prime powers (Hensel), combined by CRT
  check: 1^2 = 1, 4^2 = 1, 11^2 = 1, 14^2 = 1 (mod 15); brute force over 0..14: 4 solutions
> sqrtmod 4 45
x^2 = 4 mod 45: x = 2, 7, 38, 43
  how: 45 = 3^2 * 5: roots mod each prime (Tonelli-Shanks), lifted to the prime powers (Hensel), combined by CRT
  check: 2^2 = 4, 7^2 = 4, 38^2 = 4, 43^2 = 4 (mod 45); brute force over 0..44: 4 solutions
> sqrtmod 1 561
x^2 = 1 mod 561: x = 1, 67, 188, 254, 307, 373, 494, 560
  how: 561 = 3 * 11 * 17: roots mod each prime (Tonelli-Shanks), lifted to the prime powers (Hensel), combined by CRT
  check: 1^2 = 1, 67^2 = 1, 188^2 = 1, 254^2 = 1, ... (mod 561); brute force over 0..560: 8 solutions
> qr 1
the squares mod 1: 1 of 1 residues
  0
  how: x^2 mod 1 for every x
> qr 7
the squares mod 7: 4 of 7 residues
  0, 1, 2, 4
  7 is prime: the nonzero squares are (p-1)/2 = 3, the a with (a/p) = 1
  how: x^2 mod 7 for every x
> qr 15
the squares mod 15: 6 of 15 residues
  0, 1, 4, 6, 9, 10
  how: x^2 mod 15 for every x
> qr 1001
the squares mod 1001: 168 of 1001 residues
  0, 1, 4, 9, 14, 16, 22, 23, 25, 36, 42, 49, 53, 56, 64, 77, 78, 81, 88, 91, 92, 100, 113, 114, 121, 126, 130, 133, 144, 147, 155, 165, 168, 169, 170, 179, 191, 196, 198, 207, 212, 218, 221, 224, 225, 231, 235, 246, 247, 256, 273, 287, 289, 295, 298, 302, 308, 309, 312, 322, 324, 350, 352, 361, ... (168 in all)
  how: x^2 mod 1001 for every x
